<div class="prose-custom max-w-3xl mx-auto">

<p class="lead text-xl text-gray-600 mb-8">
<strong>1 in 4 Nigerian business owners signs contracts exactly as presented.</strong> 69% worry about the financial risk in the terms they sign. 43% were hit by a non-payment dispute in the last year.
</p>

<p>These aren't our numbers — they're from Researchscape (2026), Rocket Lawyer (2025), and SMEDAN/NBS surveys. The pattern is clear: Nigerian founders, freelancers, and SMEs are signing agreements they don't fully understand, and it's costing them.</p>

<p>Enter <strong>Odera</strong> — an AI contract review tool built specifically for Nigerian businesses who sign without a lawyer. Live now at <a href="https://odera-beta.vercel.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-primary hover:underline font-medium">odera-beta.vercel.app</a>.</p>

</div>

<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-12">

<section class="bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8">
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">The problem: you're signing blind</h2>

<p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">Most agreements get signed without a second read. The clause that lets your client deduct "any amounts considered outstanding" with no notice? You missed it. The 12-month probation with termination on one week's notice? You thought it was standard. The IP assignment that hands over work you haven't been paid for? You didn't catch it.</p>

<p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">Odera was built for <em>the people who sign without a lawyer</em>:</p>

<ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-600">
<li><strong>Freelancers</strong> — Protect your payment and your work. Catch scope creep, late-payment clauses, and IP assignments that hand over work you haven't been paid for.</li>
<li><strong>Startups</strong> — Spot liability and IP traps before you sign. Founders agreements, vendor terms, and client contracts all carry clauses that quietly cost equity or ownership.</li>
<li><strong>SMEs</strong> — Catch one-sided terms in supplier and partner deals: uncapped liability, unilateral price changes, and termination rights that only one side holds.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section>
<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6">How it works: three steps, ~60 seconds</h2>

